  "problem": "Which of the following probabilities could be approximated using the normal approximation of the binomial distribution?\n\nI. The probability of getting $5$ twos on $15$ rolls of a $6$-sided die.\n\nII. The probability of finding more than $5$ defective pairs of shoes in a random sample of $50$ if $3%$ of the pairs are defective.\n\nIII. The probability of getting more than $40$ \"yes\" answers on a yes/no survey in a randomly selected sample of $150$ people if the probability that a person answers \"yes\" is $0.5.$",
